  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alaska federal contract obligations totaled $147M in FY2027 to date. Alaska had 645 awards with an average award size of $228K. Obligations fell 96.9% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows much larger annual totals in prior years: FY22 was $3.3B, FY23 was $3.9B, FY24 was $3.9B, FY25 was $4B, and FY26 was $4.7B. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The Department of Homeland Security led buying in FY2027 to date with $122M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $13.7M and the Department of Agriculture with $11.2M. Gilbane Federal received $114M in obligations, making Gilbane Federal the single largest vendor in Alaska so far this fiscal year. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations at $120M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $15.1M. This snapshot highlights a sharp drop in obligations year to date compared with full prior fiscal years, concentrated buying by a few agencies, and a small set of vendors capturing the largest shares of current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 spending compare to prior years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $147M, a steep decline from prior full-year totals. FY26 obligations were $4.7B, FY25 obligations were $4B, FY24 obligations were $3.9B, FY23 obligations were $3.9B, and FY22 obligations were $3.3B. Obligations fell 96.9% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 buying in Alaska?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $122M, making DHS the dominant buyer so far this year. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $13.7M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $11.2M. Gilbane Federal received $114M, and Bering Straits Professional Services, LLC received $12.3M, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounting for $120M in industry obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
